@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@accessToken = pega_aqui_el_access_token

### Cambia baseUrl al endpoint API Gateway para el modo AWS serverless y usa un token de Cognito.
### Pedido correcto: local termina en COMPLETADO; AWS serverless termina en PAGADO
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "alumno@example.com",
  "sku": "POLERA-DUOC-M",
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 9990
}

### Consultar el pedido: reemplaza {id} por el id devuelto arriba
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{id}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Error esperado: HTTP 400 por correo inválido
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "correo-invalido",
  "sku": "POLERA-DUOC-M",
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 9990
}

### DLQ SQS local: se envía a las DLQ de pago e inventario
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "alumno@example.com",
  "sku": "falla",
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 1000
}

### DLQ SQS serverless: la Lambda falla intencionalmente y agota los reintentos
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "alumno@example.com",
  "sku": "FALLA-123",
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 1000
}
